changed?

Btw. There are different kinds of bugs in a program:

Heisenbugs that disapper when you examine them. Main reason being that 
debugging environment is different from release environment. These can 
be found by reading the code.

Bohrbugs exist no matter what. These are easiest to find and can be 
found by reading the code.

Mandelbugs are so chaotic that you don't even really know if there is one.

Schroedinbugs are bugs that manifest themselves only after program has 
been used unusual way when a programmer finds out that it shouldn't have 
worked at all. After the correction it stops working.

You might want to read more of these from here:

http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unusual_software_bug

